# Locale

Cursor **rules** are always **English** (instructions to the agent). Do not write new `.cursor/rules` in another language.

User-facing prose — Coordinator lines, questions, summaries, offers — uses:

`DATA_DIR/settings/locale.json` (see `coordinator/workspace.mdc`)

| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `chat_language` | ISO 639-1 (`en`, `ru`, …). How to speak to the human. |
| `docs_language` | ISO 639-1. Language of new files in `DOCS_DIR`. |

If the file or a field is missing, use `en`.

Do not translate: `task_id`, branch names, repo names, paths, shell commands, code.

Do not switch language because the latest message is in another language, unless the human explicitly asks. Persistent change = edit `locale.json`.

The Coordinator speaks under his own name (`Отто` / `Otto`, from `settings/coordinator.json` — see `coordinator/name.mdc`), rendered in `chat_language`. Templates in other rules are English **shapes** — render them in `chat_language`.
